{title: Pass Me Not, O Gentle Savior}
{artist: Fanny Crosby & William Doane}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 76}

Verse 1
[G]Pass me not, O [C]gentle [G]Savior — hear my humble [D]cry;
[G]while on others [C]thou art [G]calling, [D]do not pass me [G]by.

Chorus
[G]Savior, [C]Savior, [G]hear my humble [D]cry;
[G]while on others [C]thou art [G]calling, [D]do not pass me [G]by.

Verse 2
Let me at Thy throne of mercy
Find a sweet relief,
Kneeling there in deep contrition;
Help my unbelief.
Savior, Savior, Hear my humble cry;
While on others Thou art calling,
Do not pass me by.

Verse 3
3, Trusting only in Thy merit,
Would I seek Thy face;
Heal my wounded, broken spirit,
Save me by Thy grace.
Savior, Savior, Hear my humble cry;
While on others Thou art calling,
Do not pass me by.

Verse 4
Thou the Spring of all my comfort,
More than life to me,
Whom have I on earth beside
Thee? Whom in Heav'n but Thee?
Savior, Savior, Hear my humble cry;
While on others Thou art calling,
Do not pass me by.
